  "title": "Oil at a 5-Month High: The Week's 5 Biggest Stories",
  "description": "Five stories shaped the week of October 19 to 25, 2026: Alberta's vote against starting a separation process, the deadly attack on a funeral at a church in Jordan, Putin's agreement in principle, per the Kremlin, to resume Ukraine talks, reported planning for new strikes on Iran, and claims of tanker attacks near the Strait of Hormuz as Brent crude reached a five-month high. This recap shows who said what, what is confirmed and what is only claimed.\n\nSources:\nAl Jazeera: Alberta voters reject separation (Oct 20, 2026)\nThe Globe and Mail: The Alberta referendum by the numbers\nNPR: Gunmen open fire at a church during a funeral in Jordan (Oct 24, 2026)\nAl Jazeera: Who was behind the deadly church shooting in Jordan? (Oct 24, 2026)\nFox News: Jordan church attack in Karak kills 9 at a Greek Orthodox funeral\nAP: Trump envoy Witkoff meets Putin in St. Petersburg for Ukraine war talks (Oct 21, 2026)\nAP: Putin agrees to resume trilateral talks on Ukraine war with Kyiv and Washington: Kremlin\nFrance 24: Ukraine and Russia both say ready to resume trilateral talks with US (Oct 21, 2026)\nAP: Blaze at St Petersburg oil sites as Kyiv launches more than 1,000 drones at Russia (Oct 18, 2026)\nAxios: Military ordered to be ready for possible Iran strikes as Trump weighs timing (Oct 7, 2026)\nAxios: Trump rules out Iran strikes before midterms (Oct 8, 2026)\nAl Jazeera: Is Trump signalling a return to war with Iran after the midterms? (Oct 9, 2026)\nNew York Times (as cited by Axios, Al Jazeera and Israeli media): options for renewed Iran strikes\ni24 News: report that the US pressed Israel to strike Iran ahead of elections (Ben Caspit)\nABC News: background on the war that began Feb 28, 2026\nPetra (Jordan News Agency), via Latin Times: national mourning\nCBS News live updates: Trump accuses Iran of making up fake strikes on ships (Oct 22, 2026)\nThe Washington Times: Trump rejects Iranian claims of tanker strikes in Strait of Hormuz as oil prices rise (Oct 22, 2026)\ngCaptain: Iran claims more ships struck near Hormuz as Trump accuses Tehran of faking hits\nSplash247: Hormuz attacks overwhelm UKMTO\nU.S. Energy Information Administration (EIA): World Oil Transit Chokepoints\n\n#geopolitics #news #weeklyrecap #Iran #Ukraine",
